# Leak-guard allowlist -- scripts/ci/prepush/leak_guard.sh, check 2, rule B.
#
# Files that carry an absolute deployment-account home path BY DESIGN, where
# refusing every added line with one means the file cannot be edited at all
# (VOYN-W0-AICC-LEAK-GUARD-BLOCKS-FILES-THAT-ALREADY-CARRY-HOME-PATHS). This
# is deliberately tiny: everywhere else -- code, docs, tests -- an added home
# path is still refused unless the same path is already in the base version
# of that same file (rule A).
#
# Format, one entry per line:   <glob> <TOKEN>
#   <glob>   shell glob against the repository-relative path. `*` spans
#            directory separators, so `ops/ci/**` covers every depth under it.
#   <TOKEN>  which home root the entry permits. WORKER_HOME is the only token
#            the guard implements -- the deployment account root, already
#            public in these files by design. There is deliberately NO token
#            for personal machine home roots: those are refused everywhere,
#            allowlist or not. An unknown token makes the guard refuse.
# `#` starts a comment line. Blank lines are ignored.
#
# The guard reads this file from the BASE commit, never from the working
# tree: a branch cannot widen the guard that is judging it. A new entry is
# live only once it has landed on the base branch through review.

# The installer-integration fixture builds a clone at the worker's real path
# and bind-mounts it into the container -- the path IS the thing under test.
ops/ci/** WORKER_HOME

# systemd units: WorkingDirectory=, EnvironmentFile=, BindReadOnlyPaths= and
# the ExecStart lines of the preprod lane all name the deployment account's
# tree; a unit cannot be expressed without it.
deploy/systemd/** WORKER_HOME
